# ATAK 5.6 plugin — component-level ignores.
#
# This file previously duplicated ~90% of the root .gitignore and was byte-identical to
# ATAK5.7/.gitignore (2,100 b each) — four files, two distinct contents (audit Appendix E
# §2.4). It has been collapsed to its genuine deltas. Everything else — Gradle/Android
# build output, keystores, IDE state, OS junk, logs — is covered once at the repository
# root and must not be restated here, or the two copies will drift.

# ── Genuine component delta: re-include the SDK support files the build needs ─
# These are matched by root rules and re-included here as well as at the root, so that a
# `git add` run from inside ATAK5.6/ behaves identically to one run from the repo root.
!.takdev/
!.takdev/aars/
!.takdev/aars/*.aar
!buildtools/
!buildtools/atak-gradle-takdev.jar

# gradle.properties is ignored at the root (it may carry machine-specific paths or secrets
# in other components), except this one — it only sets a JVM heap size for R8, needed on any
# CI runner since a civRelease build's minification pass has hit OutOfMemoryError on the
# default heap.
!gradle.properties

# DEPRECATED — scheduled for removal under C-40, in step with the root .gitignore.
# See the note there: the blob is the public stock ATAK SDK dev key (md5
# de161723bca27d5da9dd16052ee18cae, identical to the SDK's own android_keystore), the
# finding is adjudicated MEDIUM, and removing this negation before the file is
# `git rm --cached`'d and build.gradle switched to env-var-sourced signing passwords would
# change nothing — an ignore rule does not untrack an already-tracked file.
!app/featurelink.keystore

# ── Build-tool cache with timestamp churn ────────────────────────────────────
# Covered by the root rule `**/.takdev/plugin.properties`; restated here only to mark that
# the `!.takdev/` re-include above is deliberately narrower than the whole directory.
.takdev/plugin.properties
